---
import LearnArticle from "../../components/LearnArticle.astro";
import DemoFrame from "../../components/DemoFrame.astro";
import RelatedLink from "../../components/RelatedLink.astro";
---

<LearnArticle
	href="/learn/encryption-basics"
	description="Encryption explained simply: plaintext, ciphertext, and keys, a hands-on Caesar cipher you can lock and crack, and why modern keys are so hard to guess."
	lead="Put a note in a box, lock it, and send it anywhere. Anyone can carry the box — but only someone with the right key can read what's inside."
>
	<section class="block">
		<p class="block-title">The Locked Box</p>
		<p class="block-text">
			When you send a message over the internet, it passes through lots of computers you don't own
			and people you'll never meet. It's a bit like handing a postcard to a chain of strangers —
			any of them could read it.
		</p>
		<p class="block-text">
			<em>Encryption</em> puts the message in a locked box first. The strangers can still pass the box
			along, but without the key, all they see is scrambled nonsense.
		</p>
		<p class="block-callout">
			The <a href="/learn/error-correction">Error Correction</a> page is about protecting data from{" "}
			<em>accidental</em> damage. Encryption is about protecting it from <em>unwanted eyes</em>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<p class="block-title">The Words You'll Hear</p>
		<div class="table-wrap">
			<table class="data-table">
				<tbody>
					<tr>
						<td><em>Plaintext</em></td>
						<td>The original, readable message.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><em>Ciphertext</em></td>
						<td>The scrambled version that looks like nonsense.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><em>Key</em></td>
						<td>The secret that tells you how to scramble and unscramble.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><em>Encrypt</em></td>
						<td>Lock it: turn plaintext into ciphertext.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><em>Decrypt</em></td>
						<td>Unlock it: turn ciphertext back into plaintext.</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<p class="block-title">A 2,000-Year-Old Lock</p>
		<p class="block-text">
			One of the oldest known ciphers is named after Julius Caesar, who is said to have used it for
			military messages. You move every letter a set number of places along the alphabet. With a
			key of 3, A becomes D, B becomes E, and so on:
		</p>
		<p class="caesar-example">
			<span>HELLO</span>
			<span class="caesar-example-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
			<span>KHOOR</span>
		</p>
		<p class="block-text">
			To decrypt, you move each letter back by the same amount. The key — "3" — is the secret.
		</p>
	</section>

	<DemoFrame label="Caesar cipher demo">
		<div class="cz-demo" data-cz-demo>
			<div class="demo-field">
				<label for="cz-text">Your message</label>
				<input id="cz-text" class="demo-input cz-text" type="text" maxlength="60" value="MEET ME AT NOON" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" data-cz-text />
			</div>
			<div class="demo-field">
				<label for="cz-shift">Key (shift)</label>
				<input id="cz-shift" class="demo-range" type="range" min="1" max="25" value="3" data-cz-shift />
				<output class="cz-shift-value" for="cz-shift" data-cz-shift-value>3</output>
			</div>
			<div class="cz-mode" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Lock or unlock">
				<label><input type="radio" name="cz-mode" value="encrypt" checked data-cz-mode /> Lock (encrypt)</label>
				<label><input type="radio" name="cz-mode" value="decrypt" data-cz-mode /> Unlock (decrypt)</label>
			</div>

			<div class="cz-alphabet" aria-hidden="true" data-cz-alphabet></div>

			<p class="demo-status cz-challenge-status" data-cz-challenge-status aria-live="polite"></p>
			<p class="cz-output-label">Result</p>
			<p class="cz-output" data-cz-output aria-live="polite"></p>

			<div class="demo-controls">
				<button type="button" class="demo-btn" data-cz-swap>Use result as the message</button>
				<button type="button" class="demo-btn" data-cz-challenge>Give me a secret message</button>
				<button type="button" class="demo-btn demo-btn--primary" data-cz-crack>Crack it: try every key</button>
			</div>
			<div class="cz-crack" data-cz-crack-panel hidden>
				<p class="demo-note">
					An attacker doesn't need your key — there are only 25 to try. Can you spot the one that
					reads as real words?
				</p>
				<ol class="cz-crack-list" data-cz-crack-list></ol>
			</div>
		</div>
	</DemoFrame>

	<section class="block">
		<p class="block-title">Why Caesar's Lock Is Weak</p>
		<p class="block-text">
			The Caesar cipher only has 25 possible keys. Anyone who intercepts the message can simply try
			all of them — which is exactly what the "Crack it" button does. A computer can do that faster
			than you can blink.
		</p>
		<p class="block-text">
			That's the heart of good encryption: there must be <em>so many possible keys</em> that trying
			them all is hopeless.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="block block--example">
		<p class="block-title">Modern Keys Are Made of Bits</p>
		<p class="block-text">
			Today's encryption keys are long binary numbers. As you've seen elsewhere on this site, every
			extra bit doubles the number of possibilities. A common key size is 128 bits, which gives:
		</p>
		<p class="big-number">2<sup>128</sup> ≈ 340,000,000,000,000,000,000,000,000,000,000,000,000 keys</p>
		<p class="block-text">
			That's the same enormous number as the count of IPv6 addresses. Even if every computer on
			Earth tried billions of keys a second, working through them all would take far, far longer
			than the universe has existed.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<p class="block-title">The Problem With Sharing Keys</p>
		<p class="block-text">
			Caesar's cipher, and many modern ones, use <em>the same key</em> to lock and unlock. That's
			called <em>symmetric</em> encryption. It's fast and strong — but it has a problem: before you can
			send a secret message, your friend needs a copy of the key. How do you get it to them without
			someone copying it on the way?
		</p>
		<p class="block-text">
			The clever solution uses two different keys — one for locking, one for unlocking.
		</p>
		<RelatedLink href="/learn/public-key-cryptography" label="Read next" />
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<p class="block-title">Where Encryption Protects You</p>
		<ul class="block-list">
			<li>The padlock icon next to a web address means your connection to that site is encrypted.</li>
			<li>Secure messaging apps encrypt messages so only the people in the chat can read them.</li>
			<li>Your phone encrypts what's stored on it, so a stolen phone doesn't mean stolen photos.</li>
			<li>Wi-Fi networks with a password encrypt the data travelling through the air.</li>
		</ul>
	</section>
</LearnArticle>

<script>
	const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-cz-demo]")!;
	const textInput = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-cz-text]")!;
	const shiftInput = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-cz-shift]")!;
	const shiftValue = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-cz-shift-value]")!;
	const modeInputs = root.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>("[data-cz-mode]");
	const alphabetEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-cz-alphabet]")!;
	const outputEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-cz-output]")!;
	const swapBtn = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-cz-swap]")!;
	const crackBtn = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-cz-crack]")!;
	const crackPanel = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-cz-crack-panel]")!;
	const crackList = root.querySelector<HTMLOListElement>("[data-cz-crack-list]")!;
	const challengeBtn = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-cz-challenge]")!;
	const challengeStatus = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-cz-challenge-status]")!;
	const SECRETS = [
		"THE KEY IS UNDER THE MAT",
		"MEET ME BY THE OLD OAK TREE",
		"BINARY IS JUST ONES AND ZEROS",
		"NEVER SHARE YOUR PASSWORD",
		"THE BOX IS LOCKED TIGHT",
		"LUNCH IS AT NOON TODAY",
	];

	const A = "A".charCodeAt(0);

	function shiftText(text: string, shift: number): string {
		// Letters move around the alphabet (wrapping Z back to A); anything
		// else — spaces, digits, punctuation — passes through unchanged.
		return text
			.toUpperCase()
			.split("")
			.map((ch) => {
				const code = ch.charCodeAt(0);
				if (code < A || code > A + 25) return ch;
				return String.fromCharCode(A + ((((code - A + shift) % 26) + 26) % 26));
			})
			.join("");
	}

	function mode(): "encrypt" | "decrypt" {
		return (Array.from(modeInputs).find((i) => i.checked)?.value as "encrypt" | "decrypt") ?? "encrypt";
	}

	function render() {
		const shift = Number(shiftInput.value);
		shiftValue.textContent = String(shift);
		const signed = mode() === "encrypt" ? shift : -shift;
		outputEl.textContent = shiftText(textInput.value, signed) || " ";

		const letters = Array.from({ length: 26 }, (_, i) => String.fromCharCode(A + i));
		alphabetEl.innerHTML = letters
			.map((letter) => `<span class="cz-pair"><span>${letter}</span><span>${shiftText(letter, signed)}</span></span>`)
			.join("");

		if (!crackPanel.hidden) renderCrack();
	}

	function renderCrack() {
		const ciphertext = mode() === "encrypt" ? outputEl.textContent ?? "" : textInput.value.toUpperCase();
		crackList.innerHTML = "";
		for (let key = 1; key <= 25; key++) {
			const li = document.createElement("li");
			const keyLabel = document.createElement("span");
			keyLabel.className = "cz-crack-key";
			keyLabel.textContent = `Key ${key}`;
			const attempt = document.createElement("span");
			attempt.textContent = shiftText(ciphertext, -key);
			li.append(keyLabel, attempt);
			crackList.append(li);
		}
	}

	textInput.addEventListener("input", render);
	shiftInput.addEventListener("input", render);
	modeInputs.forEach((i) => i.addEventListener("change", render));

	swapBtn.addEventListener("click", () => {
		textInput.value = (outputEl.textContent ?? "").trim();
		// Flip direction so pressing this after locking shows how to unlock.
		const next = mode() === "encrypt" ? "decrypt" : "encrypt";
		modeInputs.forEach((i) => (i.checked = i.value === next));
		render();
	});

	// Challenge: load a message locked with a random key, switch to Unlock,
	// and let the student slide the key until it reads as English.
	challengeBtn.addEventListener("click", () => {
		const secret = SECRETS[Math.floor(Math.random() * SECRETS.length)];
		const key = 1 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 25);
		textInput.value = shiftText(secret, key);
		modeInputs.forEach((i) => (i.checked = i.value === "decrypt"));
		shiftInput.value = "1";
		crackPanel.hidden = true;
		crackBtn.textContent = "Crack it: try every key";
		render();
		challengeStatus.textContent =
			"Here's a locked message. Slide the key until the result makes sense — that's the secret key. (Stuck? Press “Crack it”.)";
	});

	crackBtn.addEventListener("click", () => {
		crackPanel.hidden = !crackPanel.hidden;
		crackBtn.textContent = crackPanel.hidden ? "Crack it: try every key" : "Hide the cracking attempts";
		if (!crackPanel.hidden) renderCrack();
	});

	render();
</script>

<style>
	.caesar-example {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		margin: 0.5rem 0 0.75rem;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 1.3rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.12em;
		color: #fff3d6;
	}

	.caesar-example-arrow {
		color: var(--color-accent);
		letter-spacing: 0;
	}

	.big-number {
		margin: 0.5rem 0 0.75rem;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		color: #fff3d6;
		overflow-wrap: anywhere;
	}
</style>

<style is:global>
	.cz-demo .cz-text {
		width: min(100%, 22em);
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.05em;
	}

	.cz-demo .cz-shift-value {
		min-width: 2em;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 1.3em;
		color: #fff3d6;
	}

	.cz-demo .cz-mode {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		justify-content: center;
		gap: 0.5em 1.5em;
		margin-top: 0.75em;
		font-size: 0.95em;
		color: var(--color-text);
	}

	.cz-demo .cz-mode label {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.5em;
		min-height: 2.2em;
		cursor: pointer;
	}

	.cz-demo .cz-mode input {
		width: 1.1em;
		height: 1.1em;
		accent-color: var(--color-accent);
	}

	.cz-demo .cz-alphabet {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(1.9em, 1fr));
		gap: 0.25em;
		margin: 1em auto 0;
		max-width: 52em;
	}

	.cz-demo .cz-pair {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		padding: 0.25em 0;
		border-radius: 6px;
		background: var(--color-bg);
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 0.9em;
		line-height: 1.35;
	}

	.cz-demo .cz-pair span:first-child {
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
	}

	.cz-demo .cz-pair span:last-child {
		color: var(--color-accent);
	}

	.cz-demo .cz-output-label {
		margin: 1em 0 0.25em;
		text-align: center;
		font-size: 0.78em;
		font-weight: 700;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
	}

	.cz-demo .cz-output {
		margin: 0 auto;
		max-width: 30em;
		padding: 0.5em 0.75em;
		border-radius: 10px;
		background: var(--color-bg);
		border: 1px solid var(--color-accent);
		text-align: center;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 1.4em;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		color: #fff3d6;
		overflow-wrap: anywhere;
	}

	.cz-demo .cz-crack-list {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, 17em), 1fr));
		gap: 0.25em 1em;
		margin: 0.75em 0 0;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.9em;
		color: var(--color-text);
	}

	.cz-demo .cz-crack-list li {
		display: flex;
		gap: 0.75em;
		padding: 0.25em 0.5em;
		border-radius: 6px;
		background: var(--color-bg);
		overflow-wrap: anywhere;
	}

	.cz-demo .cz-crack-key {
		flex-shrink: 0;
		min-width: 4em;
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
	}
</style>
